{
 "provenance": {
  "command": "cd apps/mobile && MINDWTR_CAPTURE_ENTRY_POINTS=1 MINDWTR_CAPTURE_ENTRY_POINTS_COMMIT=$(git rev-parse HEAD) TZ=UTC bunx vitest run tests/entry-points.parity.test.tsx",
  "capturedAt": "127631b0e2c559e9660b46c5c10de4f2dbdcf2c0",
  "sourceState": "Every file under apps/ and packages/ was at HEAD except this entry-points parity harness and its fixture.",
  "rendering": "Platform.OS is android. useRootLayoutExternalCapture runs under react-test-renderer with canonical data ready, one delivery per link or share, and a router that cannot go back; the store holds `store`. resolveText is core's translateWithFallback over the English strings. A share is read by expo-share-intent's parseShareIntent from the payload its Android module sends for ACTION_SEND text/plain.",
  "amendments": [
   "shares: the email share (subject 'Subject', body 'Body with https://example.com/doc') no longer repeats the body's link in the description (RN bug fix after the capture: buildShareCaptureDraft adds the link only when the body does not hold it).",
   "urls: the two task links that open no task (mindwtr:///open?task=t-deleted, mindwtr://open?task=missing) now show the error toast 'This task is not in this library...' (#1368 a7941b1c6 added it); recaptured at capturedAt, no other observation changed.",
   "urls: #1553 changes redirectWarm to an empty path for the eight valid entity links so the incoming handler owns navigation; redirectCold and all other observations stay unchanged. Amended after 6876ac0fe6e04ec66665255e462e3fe35a7d8db7 and verified by the RN and core entry-point replay tests."
  ]
 },
